1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,600
Placement season. Same details, different form, every single drive.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:11,400
I think there is a better way, and I have been building it.

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:16,200
If you have been through campus placements, you know the pattern.

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:22,800
You type your CGPA, 10th and 12th percentages, backlogs and links.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Then you do it again.

6
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:33,600
And somewhere in between you wonder: am I even eligible for this?

7
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:41,000
I am an independent founder. There is no company behind this yet, no customer list, no big numbers to show.

8
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:47,500
Just a product, and a campus pilot we are preparing.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
I would rather tell you that than make something up.

10
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:01,000
UpGrid is a student-first app. You build your profile once.

11
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:07,300
A completion meter tells you what is missing and what to do next.

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:17,500
Academics, links, skills, preferences, and up to five resume links.

13
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:28,800
Each academic field shows whether it is unverified, self-reported, or verified by your placement officer.

14
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:36,200
Then you see drives. Each one is checked against your profile.

15
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:41,800
The app shows the reason, not just a result.

16
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:48,600
Criterion by criterion: required versus yours.

17
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:53,800
No guessing, no silent rejection.

18
00:01:54,600 --> 00:02:04,000
Eligible, not eligible, or pending (Check profile) when something is missing.

19
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:10,500
Applying is a review, not a typing session.

20
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:15,400
You see what will be shared and where each value came from.

21
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:24,700
You answer only the extra questions, and choose a resume.

22
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:29,500
Accept the declarations and opt in.

23
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
You get a reference number and a timeline.

24
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:39,200
Tap twice by accident and you will not apply twice.

25
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:44,500
And deadlines. Reminders arrive 60, 30 and 15 minutes before.

26
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:48,300
By push and in the app. Once you apply, they stop.

27
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:54,200
Switch any off. Choose push, in-app, or both.

28
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,400
Set quiet hours that suit you.

29
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:05,300
For placement cells: a drive wizard with autosaved drafts and a check before publishing.

30
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:09,900
An eligible-student count, with reasons.

31
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:14,700
An applicant pipeline from submitted to joined.

32
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:19,200
And announcements.

33
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:25,500
UpGrid is launching soon, starting with a campus pilot.

34
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:30,500
Students: join the waitlist. Placement cells: message me about a pilot.

35
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:34,200
Link in the description. Thanks for watching.

